libc: expose the toolchain pthread types to picolibc C++ builds

The SDK's components/libc/sys/types.h shadows the toolchain header and
skips <sys/_pthreadtypes.h> whenever __PICOLIBC__ is defined. The
bouffalolab/toolchain GCC 14.3 libstdc++ uses POSIX gthreads, so C++
standard headers that reach the toolchain <pthread.h> (for example
<mutex>) fail with "'pthread_mutexattr_t' was not declared". Include the
toolchain pthread types when the header exists; picolibc builds without
it keep the old behaviour.

Applies to components/libc/sys/types.h of bouffalo_sdk v2.3.38 (946f92a0).
Drop this patch when sources.json moves to a release that includes it.

--- a/components/libc/sys/types.h
+++ b/components/libc/sys/types.h
@@ -221,7 +221,8 @@
 
 #include <sys/features.h>
 #ifndef CONFIG_POSIX
-#ifndef __PICOLIBC__
+/* libstdc++ gthreads in GCC 14.3 (picolibc) need the toolchain pthread types. */
+#if !defined(__PICOLIBC__) || __has_include(<sys/_pthreadtypes.h>)
 #include <sys/_pthreadtypes.h>
 #endif
 #endif
